  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The identity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mn>90</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> reduces the equation to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>. Equal cosines give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mn>360</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mrow></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mn>360</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>360</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mrow></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>40</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>. On the given closed interval, the first family contributes only 0 and 360, both already in the second family.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> The distinct solutions are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x02026;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>360</mn></mrow></math> degrees: ten terms. Their sum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>360</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1800</mn></mrow></math> degrees. Answer B.</p>"
